  "original_patch_has_test_hunk": true,
  "source_conclusion": "The complete no-data OnPush fix is inherited through the actual public CdkTable parent on this branch. Both authenticated minimum renderer implementations mark the owning view after no-data visibility transitions; owned MatLegacyTable overrides neither renderer nor render subscription, and its public datasource/outlet/no-data routes reach that parent. The earlier marker/replay-only inheritance statement remains historical. Qualification requires the exact current packed Angular OnPush case, not ancestry or a mark-call spy. No packed/native, G11 or security pass is asserted here. Constructor-source requalification: the only owned table edits add a local class decorator/import. Its exact reviewed helper constructs the genuine public CdkTable with the original new.target and node services, suppressing only the optional viewport during parent construction. The change-detector request is forwarded to the original node context, and no render/data-source/no-data method is overridden. Existing table metadata, outlets and rendering bodies are unchanged. This preserves the source delegation claim; real current packed OnPush rendering remains mandatory.",
  "hunk_reviews": [
    {
      "hunk": 1,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.spec.ts",
      "judgment": "The ChangeDetectionStrategy import enables the added OnPush test component; it has no runtime library effect."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 2,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.spec.ts",
      "judgment": "The new regression keeps the child datasource input object stable, empties its data through the parent and requires a bound colspan value. The mandatory legacy case preserves that trigger and parent-only detection, adding restored/repeated-empty states, class/text assertions and teardown."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 3,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.spec.ts",
      "judgment": "The new parent/OnPush child creates the real change-detection boundary. The legacy case uses actual owned/public table and no-data provider identities. Its dynamic colspan is on the native td alongside interpolation within the same no-data embedded view, preserving valid legacy cell structure while requiring view update. A static row or mark-call spy cannot satisfy this case."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 4,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.ts",
      "judgment": "The data outlet constructor is reformatted only. The ViewContainerRef/ElementRef parameter order, public parameter properties and empty constructor body remain unchanged; this hunk introduces no behavior or compatibility requirement."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 5,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.ts",
      "judgment": "The header outlet constructor is reformatted only. The ViewContainerRef/ElementRef parameter order, public parameter properties and empty constructor body remain unchanged; this hunk introduces no behavior or compatibility requirement."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 6,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.ts",
      "judgment": "The footer outlet constructor is reformatted only. The ViewContainerRef/ElementRef parameter order, public parameter properties and empty constructor body remain unchanged; this hunk introduces no behavior or compatibility requirement."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 7,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.ts",
      "judgment": "The no-data outlet constructor is reformatted only. The ViewContainerRef/ElementRef parameter order, public parameter properties and empty constructor body remain unchanged; this hunk introduces no behavior or compatibility requirement."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 8,
      "file": "src/cdk/table/table.ts",
      "judgment": "The only runtime addition marks the owning change detector after no-data visibility state changes. Both exact minimum public CdkTable implementations retain it. The datasource subscription calls renderRows; both changed and unchanged render paths call _updateNoDataRow. That inherited method creates/clears the no-data view then marks the owner. MatLegacyTable overrides none of these methods. Its outlet adapter supplies public view/element references and its no-data provider supplies the same owned directive to public parent queries. Actual Angular OnPush child checking remains a mandatory artifact requirement."
    }
  ],
